  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the sum of outcomes regardless of probabilities, but the individual's verbal report emphasizes the probability of losing (i.e., the 50% chance of a negative outcome in Lottery B). The information considered by the individual (probability of loss) is unrelated to the information required by the decision reason (sum of outcomes). Furthermore, the justification based on risk aversion and fear of loss contrasts with the rule of the decision reason, which would treat both lotteries equally due to their equal outcome sums. There is no indication that the individual calculated or considered the sum of outcomes. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
